1.2 - [RELEASEDATE]
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

- Changed: Passwords are hashed with password_hash() instead of unsalted MD5.
  Stored MD5 hashes are still accepted and replaced with a new hash on the
  next successful login, unless the new option rehashPasswords is false.
- Fixed: generatePassword() uses random_int() instead of a predictable seed.
- Fixed: createUser() quotes the column names of $extraInfo and the configured
  table and field names.
- Fixed: No md5( null ) deprecation when the user is taken from the session.
- Added: zetacomponents/authentication-database-tiein as a dependency.

Upgrading: the password column of the user table must hold at least 60
characters, 255 are recommended because the length of PASSWORD_DEFAULT hashes
can grow. A column sized for MD5 hashes (VARCHAR(32)) has to be widened. Until
then a legacy hash is kept when the database rejects or truncates the new one,
and logins keep working with it; set the option rehashPasswords to false to
avoid the extra queries.


